==[ AmmoCode Documentation ]==================================================

This is the technical reference for AmmoCode objects to be used with GunCode
and MagazineCode.

AmmoCode inherits NewGlobCode, which inherits NewThingCode, so functions like
set_value(), set_gettable(), and such are all defined and declared in
new_thing.c or new_glob.c

Any questions, bug reports, spelling corrections, or enhancement requests
should be addressed to Deathdealer.

=====[ Set Functions ]========================================================

void set_max_damage( int max )

     Used to set the ammo's maximum damage per shot.
     Default: 5


void set_min_damage( int min )

     Used to set the ammo's minimum damage per shot.
     Default: 3


void set_damage( int min, int max )

     This function merely passes <min> and <max> to the corresponing function
     above, but it is included for its usefulness.
     

void set_ammo_type( string type )

     Used to set the ammunition type of the round.  Any gun or magazine the
     ammo is meant to be loaded into must have a matching <type>.
     Default: ".22 caliber"


void set_damage_type( string type )

     Used to set the ammo's damage type when a hit is scored in combat.
     Default: "piercing"

void set_jam_chance( int jam )

     Used to set the ammo's extra jam chance when being fired from a gun.
     Bullets that perform special functions or do excessive amounts of
     damage should have a higher <jam> chance as they will tend to be
     oddly shaped or bulkier than standard rounds.
     Default: 0


void set_extra_delay( int delay )

     Used to set the bullets extra combat delay when loading into a gun or
     magazine.  If the round is large, oddly shaped, or particularly heavy it
     will tend to be more difficult to load, the extra <delay> will reflect
     this.
     Default: 0


=====[ Query Functions ]======================================================

int query_max_damage()

     Returns the rounds maximum damage.


int query_min_damage()

     Returns the rounds minimum damage.


string query_ammo_type()

     Returns the rounds ammo type.


string query_damage_type()

     Returns the rounds damage type.


int query_jam_chance()

     Returns the rounds extra chance of jamming when be fired from a gun.


int query_extra_delay()

     Returns the rounds extra combat delay when being loaded into a gun or
     magazine.


=====[ Optional Functions ]===================================================

void extra_hit( object attacker, object target )

     Overload this function if you want the round to do something special
     when it hits a target (ie, poison them, set them on fire, knock them
     down, etc...).


void extra_message( object attacker, object target )

     Overload this function when you want the round to print out an additional
     combat message when fired.  For instance, a magazine might have tracers
     loaded as the last few rounds to let the gun wielder know that they will
     need to reload the weapon soon.

